hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1433","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abdul Wahhab told us, Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He said: “He would focus the spear on the Day of Breakfast and Sacrifice and pray to it, and he would deliver the sermon after the prayer.”"
"1434","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Khalid, who is Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was going out on the day of the breaking of the fast. And on the Day of Sacrifice, he sticks the spear between his hands when he stands and prays.”"
